# Monorepo agent routing

1. Read [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) first for Git ownership, secrets, and production authorization boundaries.
2. For Google Apps Script work (CLASP, libraries, solutions, deploy/rollback), follow [skills/gas-monorepo-engineer/SKILL.md](../../skills/gas-monorepo-engineer/SKILL.md) and load skill references only when needed. For GAS **runtime** validation, read [gas-runtime-execution.md](../../skills/gas-monorepo-engineer/references/gas-runtime-execution.md)—do not default to `clasp run` / `scripts.run`.
3. Load [docs/agent/monorepo-reference.md](../../docs/agent/monorepo-reference.md) and [config/apps.json](../../config/apps.json) when you need application maps, commands, or portal metadata — not for every trivial edit.
4. Keep [.cursorrules](../../.cursorrules) coding conventions; do not duplicate the full skill or monorepo documentation here.

## Worktree inventory (substantial tasks)

Before substantial edits: inventory the full working tree (tracked, staged, untracked); classify paths as in-scope, pre-existing unrelated, generated/ignored, or needs investigation; **preserve unrelated user work** (do not revert or stage unrelated paths to “clean” status).

Before reporting completion: inventory again; commit and push all intended in-scope changes; account for every remaining dirty path; never report task completion with unexplained task-related modifications left unstaged or uncommitted.
